      "text": "The base operator `op` was built on only `j-i-1` (5) qubits. The `qargs` list then points at qubits 3 to 7, which do not exist on a 5-qubit operator. That makes the internal einsum indices go out of range, which produces the confusing `subscript is not within the valid range` error. The fix is to build `op` as the full `N`-qubit identity, so `opZ` can be placed on qubits `i+1 … j-1`.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Operator\n\ni, j, N = 2, 8, 10\n# FIX: base operator had only j-i-1 qubits -> use 'I' * N, because qargs range(i+1, j) refers to qubits of the full N-qubit system and must lie within the operator\nop = Operator.from_label('I' * N)\nopZ = Operator.from_label('Z' * (j - i - 1))\nop = op._add(opZ, qargs=list(range(i + 1, j)))\n\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
